A||N||4||Vlad||Battery tray ground.||||5||
Z||000000||Vlad||09-19-2000||02:34 AM||||Because of bed noise coming from rusted battery tray, I went deep down there to fix it and what I found was a rusted in two points tray (I got rid of what was left of the baskets) and cut wire which I think was a ground wire.<P>Now while fixing the tray seems to be a separate job, how do I fix a ground wire? Does it really have to be fixed?<P>Since I don't have a ground wire any more, where should I put a new one. Between what parts?<P><BR>Thanks<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||09-19-2000||08:26 AM||||You can connect your ground to the right engine lid hinge box.  If you have a v-6 there should be a ground strap attached there already that goes to the intake upper plenum.  I'm not sure if the L-4 has the same ground.<P>BTW.  I just picked up a new battery tray and battery support from a local Pontiac dealer.  One was $12.99 US and the other was $11.00 US and they are still available.  I'll bolt the support back to good metal on the firewall and fender well.  It has the hole for the ground wire.<P>Hope this helps,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||Vlad||09-19-2000||11:24 AM||||Thanks for replay.<P>I have  V6. So what you mean is to connect a wire from negative terminal of battery to the thik metal wire coming from from behind the engine and hooked to the engine lid?<P>The reason I ask is that I didn't have that wire at all. One of previos owners removed it. The car was without that ground wire for god knows how long.......<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||Brian84SE||09-19-2000||12:05 PM||||I just got a tray and support from the fiero store.  They were both about $20 each. Geez...should have went to the dealer!||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnnyK||09-19-2000||03:55 PM||||Yeah, I put in a new battery tray but never connected the ground wire, because it was too much work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (The screw was rusted to the wire, so it wouldn;t turn without the wire wrapping around and around, so I figured, what the heck, I don't need.. I didn't want to waste my 2 minutes fixing it..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Wonder what negative effects that can have?||||reg||1
